{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-05 design finalized and explicitly approved against origin/main 3b34d8b449ae4b56a5da8fb434aa75df7194b0c4 (2026-08-18).\n\nApproved end state: one stdlib-only immutable lazy command registry; every stable verb remains discoverable; every visible top-level command has canonical package-data help; overview/help/alias/unknown routing occurs before RP-04 operation-snapshot composition, config materialization, store mount, handler resolution, and optional imports. Exact aliases reuse canonical help; compatibility shims retain alias-specific help naming the replacement; hidden bridge-status resolves explicit help but remains undiscoverable; purge-bridge remains unknown. Nested parsing stays handler-owned. Semantic capabilities map to packaging extras and one of error/unavailable/abstain/fallback, but enforcement occurs only after the selected mode/backend is known and domain components retain their result shapes.\n\nImplementation defaults accepted with the design: frozen dataclasses/typed enums; exact aliases embedded in routes (no alias chains); pure runtime validation for duplicate spellings, policy contradictions, unknown capability names, help-resource census, and retired-token collisions; full-extra CI—not normal startup—resolves every module:function handler/selector; compatibility exports are derived from the registry during expand/contract migration; docs/reference and discovery checks enumerate the registry; no plugin discovery, second argument parser, DI container, or middleware framework.\n\nAdversarial critique: validating handler strings during ordinary startup would defeat lazy imports, so reference resolution is isolated to the full-extra contract lane; capability policy is descriptive/shared-error infrastructure only, so metrics/grounding/rich-text fallbacks remain domain-owned; the 714-line current facade requires a dedicated registry module under the 800-line cap. Focused current-main baseline: 69 passed, 11 skipped; CLI-reference generation current; no heavy optional modules imported by rebar._cli.\n\nDependency: implementation is blocked on RP-04 contract completion (vibrant-legal-hind, especially junior-lepidolite-boa) because its centralized operation-composition cutover owns overlapping src/rebar seams. Recovery authority remains irascible-clueless-basenji; local detail remains .joe-janitor/rp05-cli-registry-research.md."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787069480993616001,"uuid":"9a4d62cf-1a5d-4381-92a4-987d67d7c07d"}